<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>The Guardian's Awakening</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <div class="container">
            <h1>The Guardian's Awakening</h1>
            <p class="author">A Tale of Magic and Destiny</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <div class="container">
            <ul class="nav-links">
                <li><a href="#">Library</a></li>
                <li><a href="#">Bookmarks</a></li>
                <li><a href="#">Discover</a></li>
                <li><a href="#">Settings</a></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <main>
        <aside class="chapters">
            <h2>Chapters</h2>
            <ul class="chapter-list">
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link active" data-chapter="1">Chapter 1: The Beginning</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="2">Chapter 2: The Journey</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="3">Chapter 3: Unexpected Events</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="4">Chapter 4: The Discovery</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="5">Chapter 5: Revelations</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="6">Chapter 6: Confrontation</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="7">Chapter 7: Resolution</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="8">Chapter 8: A New Dawn</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="9">Chapter 9: Unknown Territories</a></li>
                <li><a href="#" class="chapter-link" data-chapter="10">Chapter 10: The Final Chapter</a></li>
            </ul>
        </aside>

        <section class="content">
            <div class="progress">
                <span id="progress-percent">10%</span> • <span id="current-chapter">Chapter 1</span> of 10
            </div>
            <div id="chapter-content">
                <h3 id="chapter-title">Chapter 1: The Beginning</h3>
                <div id="chapter-text">
                    <p>It was a quiet morning in the small town of Willowbrook. The kind of quiet that settles over a place where nothing extraordinary ever happens, where the most exciting event might be the arrival of a new shipment at Henderson's General Store or Mrs. Patterson's cat getting stuck in the old oak tree again.</p>
                    
                    <p>Sarah Mitchell had lived in Willowbrook all her twenty-five years, and she had grown accustomed to this predictable rhythm of life. She worked as the town librarian, a position that perfectly suited her love of stories and quiet contemplation. Every morning, she would walk the same route to work, past the same weathered houses with their neatly trimmed gardens, greeting the same neighbors with the same polite exchanges about the weather.</p>
                    
                    <p>But this morning felt different somehow. As Sarah unlocked the heavy wooden doors of the Willowbrook Public Library, she noticed something unusual. A book lay on the front steps—an old, leather-bound volume she had never seen before. Its cover was worn smooth by countless hands, and strange symbols were etched around its edges. The title, barely visible in faded gold lettering, read "Chronicles of the Forgotten Realm."</p>
                    
                    <p>Sarah picked up the mysterious book, feeling an odd tingling sensation as her fingers touched the ancient leather. Little did she know that this simple act would set in motion a chain of events that would forever change not only her life, but the fate of Willowbrook itself.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <script>
        // Chapter content data
        const chapterData = {
            1: {
                title: "Chapter 1: The Beginning",
                content: `
                    <p>It was a quiet morning in the small town of Willowbrook. The kind of quiet that settles over a place where nothing extraordinary ever happens, where the most exciting event might be the arrival of a new shipment at Henderson's General Store or Mrs. Patterson's cat getting stuck in the old oak tree again.</p>
                    
                    <p>Sarah Mitchell had lived in Willowbrook all her twenty-five years, and she had grown accustomed to this predictable rhythm of life. She worked as the town librarian, a position that perfectly suited her love of stories and quiet contemplation. Every morning, she would walk the same route to work, past the same weathered houses with their neatly trimmed gardens, greeting the same neighbors with the same polite exchanges about the weather.</p>
                    
                    <p>But this morning felt different somehow. As Sarah unlocked the heavy wooden doors of the Willowbrook Public Library, she noticed something unusual. A book lay on the front steps—an old, leather-bound volume she had never seen before. Its cover was worn smooth by countless hands, and strange symbols were etched around its edges. The title, barely visible in faded gold lettering, read "Chronicles of the Forgotten Realm."</p>
                    
                    <p>Sarah picked up the mysterious book, feeling an odd tingling sensation as her fingers touched the ancient leather. Little did she know that this simple act would set in motion a chain of events that would forever change not only her life, but the fate of Willowbrook itself.</p>
                `
            },
            2: {
                title: "Chapter 2: The Journey",
                content: `
                    <p>That evening, Sarah sat in her small apartment above the library, the mysterious book open before her on her kitchen table. The strange symbols seemed to shimmer in the lamplight, and as she traced them with her finger, they began to glow with a soft, ethereal light.</p>
                    
                    <p>Suddenly, the pages began to turn on their own, revealing text written in a language she had never seen before. Yet, somehow, she could understand every word. The book spoke of a realm beyond the veil of ordinary reality, a place where magic still flowed like rivers and ancient guardians watched over forgotten secrets.</p>
                    
                    <p>As Sarah read deeper into the night, she discovered that Willowbrook was not the sleepy, ordinary town she had always believed it to be. According to the book, her hometown sat upon one of the few remaining doorways between the human world and the Forgotten Realm—a doorway that had been sealed centuries ago to protect both worlds from a great darkness.</p>
                    
                    <p>The book warned that the seal was weakening, and that someone with the bloodline of the ancient guardians would be needed to renew it. As Sarah read these words, a strange birthmark on her wrist—one she had always dismissed as an oddly shaped freckle—began to glow with the same ethereal light as the symbols in the book.</p>
                `
            },
            3: {
                title: "Chapter 3: Unexpected Events",
                content: `
                    <p>The next morning brought chaos to Willowbrook. Sarah woke to the sound of screams and commotion in the streets below. Looking out her window, she gasped in disbelief. Strange, luminescent creatures darted through the town square—beings that seemed to be made of pure light and shadow, moving with an otherworldly grace.</p>
                    
                    <p>The townspeople ran in panic, some taking shelter in their homes while others gathered in confused clusters, pointing at the impossible sight. Old Mr. Henderson stood frozen in front of his store, his mouth agape as one of the creatures—resembling a cross between a deer and a wisp of smoke—bounded past him without seeming to notice his presence.</p>
                    
                    <p>Sarah clutched the ancient book to her chest, understanding now that her reading had somehow triggered these events. The seal was indeed weakening, and creatures from the Forgotten Realm were beginning to slip through. She watched as more appeared throughout the town: tiny beings that looked like floating jellyfish made of starlight, and larger entities that resembled wolves crafted from moonbeams and mist.</p>
                    
                    <p>The book had mentioned that only someone with guardian blood could restore the seal, but it had also warned of great danger. As Sarah prepared to leave her apartment, she noticed that the birthmark on her wrist was now glowing so brightly that she had to cover it with her sleeve. Whatever was happening to Willowbrook, she was somehow at the center of it all.</p>
                `
            },
            4: {
                title: "Chapter 4: The Discovery",
                content: `
                    <p>Driven by instinct and the growing warmth of her birthmark, Sarah made her way through the chaotic streets toward the old Willowbrook Cemetery. The book had mentioned something about the guardian's resting place, and the cemetery was the oldest part of town, dating back to the original settlement.</p>
                    
                    <p>As she walked, the ethereal creatures seemed to part before her, as if recognizing something in her presence. An elderly woman named Mrs. Chen, who had always been known for her peculiar wisdom and herb garden, approached Sarah near the cemetery gates.</p>
                    
                    <p>"I've been waiting for this day for forty years," Mrs. Chen said quietly, her eyes reflecting an ancient knowledge. "My grandmother told me stories of the guardians, passed down through generations. She said that when the creatures returned, the last guardian would awaken." She pressed a small, intricately carved stone into Sarah's hand. "This belongs to you now. It was your great-great-grandmother's."</p>
                    
                    <p>The stone was warm to the touch and seemed to resonate with Sarah's birthmark. As she held it, memories that weren't her own began to flood her mind—images of a woman who looked remarkably like her, standing at the boundary between worlds, wielding powers that seemed to flow from the very earth itself. Sarah realized that she was the descendant of the original guardian who had sealed the doorway, and that the responsibility for protecting both worlds now fell to her.</p>
                `
            },
            5: {
                title: "Chapter 5: Revelations",
                content: `
                    <p>Deep within the cemetery, Sarah found what she was looking for: an ornate mausoleum bearing the name "Lydia Mitchell"—her ancestor. The door, which should have been locked and weathered by time, opened easily at her touch. Inside, the walls were covered with the same symbols from the ancient book, all glowing softly in response to her presence.</p>
                    
                    <p>At the center of the mausoleum stood a pedestal holding a crystal that pulsed with inner light. As Sarah approached, the book in her hands grew warm, and its pages flipped to a section she hadn't seen before—instructions for renewing the seal. But the text revealed a troubling truth: the seal hadn't just been weakening naturally. Someone had been deliberately trying to break it.</p>
                    
                    <p>The crystal showed her visions of a figure in dark robes who had been conducting rituals around the town for months, always under cover of darkness. This person sought to open the doorway permanently, allowing the darker creatures of the Forgotten Realm to enter the human world. These malevolent beings would bring chaos and destruction, feeding on fear and despair.</p>
                    
                    <p>Sarah understood now that the gentle, luminescent creatures currently roaming Willowbrook were not the real threat—they were refugees, fleeing from something far more sinister. The guardian's seal had been the only thing standing between the human world and an invasion of shadow creatures that would consume everything in their path. And someone in Willowbrook was helping them.</p>
                `
            },
            6: {
                title: "Chapter 6: Confrontation",
                content: `
                    <p>Armed with her newfound knowledge and the guardian's crystal, Sarah emerged from the mausoleum to find Willowbrook transformed. The sky had darkened to an unnatural twilight, and the air crackled with unstable magical energy. The gentle creatures from before were now huddled together in frightened groups, while something far more menacing began to seep through the cracks in reality.</p>
                    
                    <p>Shadow creatures—beings of pure malevolence that seemed to absorb light itself—were beginning to manifest throughout the town. They moved like living nightmares, leaving trails of withered grass and cracked pavement in their wake. The townspeople who had remained outside were now running in genuine terror as the temperature dropped and an oppressive feeling of dread settled over everything.</p>
                    
                    <p>At the town square, Sarah confronted the figure she had seen in her visions. To her shock, it was Mr. Aldridge, the town's respected mayor, who had always seemed so caring and community-minded. His kind demeanor had been replaced by something cold and calculating as he stood at the center of a ritual circle drawn in silver and black.</p>
                    
                    <p>"You're too late, little guardian," Aldridge sneered, his voice echoing with an otherworldly resonance. "I've spent years preparing for this moment. The Shadow King has promised me power beyond imagination in exchange for opening this doorway. Your ancestors' antiquated notions of protection will not stop progress." Dark energy swirled around him as he continued his incantations, and more shadow creatures began pouring through the growing tears in reality.</p>
                `
            },
            7: {
                title: "Chapter 7: Resolution",
                content: `
                    <p>Sarah felt the power of her guardian heritage flowing through her as she raised the crystal high. The birthmark on her wrist blazed with brilliant white light, and she could feel the strength of all the guardians who had come before her. The ancient book floating beside her, its pages turning rapidly as it provided her with the knowledge she needed to counter Aldridge's dark magic.</p>
                    
                    <p>The battle between light and shadow raged through the town square as Sarah and Aldridge faced each other. Where his dark energy withered and corrupted, her guardian light healed and restored. The gentle creatures from the Forgotten Realm gathered around her, adding their own luminous energy to hers, while the shadow creatures pressed forward, trying to overwhelm her defenses.</p>
                    
                    <p>Drawing upon the power of the guardian's crystal and the collective will of the townspeople who had gathered to witness this impossible confrontation, Sarah began the ritual to reseal the doorway. The process required her to pour her own life force into the barrier, potentially sacrificing herself to save both worlds. As the bright magic flowed from her, Aldridge's connection to the Shadow King began to weaken.</p>
                    
                    <p>In a final, desperate attempt to complete his dark ritual, Aldridge lunged forward. But the combined light of Sarah's guardian power and the loyal creatures of the Forgotten Realm was too strong. The mayor was consumed by his own shadow magic, banished to the dark realm he had tried to unleash upon the world. The doorway between worlds sealed with a brilliant flash that could be seen for miles around.</p>
                `
            },
            8: {
                title: "Chapter 8: A New Dawn",
                content: `
                    <p>As the first rays of true dawn broke over Willowbrook, the town slowly returned to normal. The shadow creatures had been banished back to their dark realm, and most of the gentle light-beings had returned to the Forgotten Realm through the now-properly sealed doorway. A few remained, choosing to live peacefully in the spaces between worlds under Sarah's guardianship.</p>
                    
                    <p>The townspeople, though shaken by what they had witnessed, rallied around their unexpected protector. Sarah found herself no longer just the quiet librarian, but a bridge between the mundane and the magical. The library became a sanctuary where she could study the ancient texts and prepare for future threats, while also helping her neighbors understand the true nature of their extraordinary town.</p>
                    
                    <p>Mrs. Chen revealed that she was part of a secret network of people who had always known about Willowbrook's special nature—descendants of those who had helped the original guardians centuries ago. They would help Sarah in her new role, providing support and wisdom as she learned to balance her responsibilities to both worlds.</p>
                    
                    <p>The ancient book, now permanently bonded to Sarah, continued to reveal new information about the guardian's duties. She learned that there were other sealed doorways around the world, each protected by guardian bloodlines, and that she was now part of an ancient network dedicated to maintaining the balance between realms. Her quiet life in Willowbrook had ended, but a much greater adventure was just beginning.</p>
                `
            },
            9: {
                title: "Chapter 9: Unknown Territories",
                content: `
                    <p>Three months after the confrontation with Aldridge, Sarah received her first communication from other guardians around the world. Through the ancient book, she learned of disturbances at other sealed doorways—in the forests of Romania, the mountains of Tibet, and the deserts of Australia. The Shadow King's influence had reached further than anyone had realized.</p>
                    
                    <p>Sarah discovered that she would need to travel to these distant locations to help strengthen the other seals and train new guardians whose bloodlines were awakening. The prospect both thrilled and terrified her—she had never traveled beyond the state borders, let alone to other continents. But the responsibility was clear, and the network of guardians depended on each other for survival.</p>
                    
                    <p>Before departing on her first journey, Sarah worked with Mrs. Chen and the other secret keepers to establish protections for Willowbrook in her absence. They set up a rotation of watchers who could alert her through the mystical connection she maintained with the town. Several of the friendly light-beings who had chosen to remain would also serve as sentinels, their otherworldly senses capable of detecting threats long before human perception could.</p>
                    
                    <p>As Sarah prepared to leave the only home she had ever known, she reflected on how much her life had changed. The quiet librarian who had once thought her greatest adventure would be organizing the annual book fair was now preparing to traverse the globe, wielding ancient magic and protecting reality itself. The unknown territories ahead were daunting, but she faced them with the courage of all the guardians who had come before her.</p>
                `
            },
            10: {
                title: "Chapter 10: The Final Chapter",
                content: `
                    <p>One year later, Sarah returned to Willowbrook as a seasoned guardian. Her travels had taken her to remarkable places and introduced her to extraordinary people—fellow guardians who had become like family, scholars of ancient magic who had helped her understand her heritage, and creatures from various realms who had chosen to fight alongside the forces of light.</p>
                    
                    <p>The network of guardians was stronger now, with several new members awakening to their destinies and taking up the mantle of protection. The threat of the Shadow King had been contained, though Sarah knew it was not permanently eliminated. Such was the nature of the guardian's duty—eternal vigilance in service of balance and protection.</p>
                    
                    <p>Willowbrook had flourished in the year since the awakening. The town now attracted visitors who sensed something special about the place, though they couldn't quite put their finger on what made it so peaceful and harmonious. A few individuals with latent magical sensitivity had even chosen to relocate there, drawn by the town's unique energy and Sarah's quiet leadership.</p>
                    
                    <p>As Sarah stood once again at the entrance to the library that had started it all, she smiled at the journey that had brought her full circle. The mysterious book that had appeared on the library steps that fateful morning now rested safely in a place of honor inside, ready to guide the next generation of guardians when their time came. She had learned that every ending was simply a new beginning in disguise, and that the greatest adventures often began with the smallest, most unexpected discoveries.</p>
                    
                    <p>The quiet morning in Willowbrook was no longer quite so quiet—it hummed with the gentle magic of a place where two worlds touched, protected by a guardian who had found her true purpose in the most unlikely of circumstances. And in the distance, barely visible to those who knew how to look, the light-beings danced in the early morning mist, a reminder that wonder and magic were never truly gone—they were simply waiting for someone brave enough to discover them.</p>
                `
            }
        };

        // Function to load a specific chapter
        function loadChapter(chapterNumber) {
            const chapter = chapterData[chapterNumber];
            if (!chapter) return;

            // Update content
            document.getElementById('chapter-title').textContent = chapter.title;
            document.getElementById('chapter-text').innerHTML = chapter.content;
            
            // Update progress
            const progress = Math.round((chapterNumber / 10) * 100);
            document.getElementById('progress-percent').textContent = progress + '%';
            document.getElementById('current-chapter').textContent = `Chapter ${chapterNumber}`;
            
            // Update active chapter in navigation
            document.querySelectorAll('.chapter-link').forEach(link => {
                link.classList.remove('active');
            });
            document.querySelector(`[data-chapter="${chapterNumber}"]`).classList.add('active');
            
            // Scroll to top of content
            document.querySelector('.content').scrollTop = 0;
        }

        // Add event listeners to chapter links
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
            document.querySelectorAll('.chapter-link').forEach(link => {
                link.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
                    e.preventDefault();
                    const chapterNumber = parseInt(this.dataset.chapter);
                    loadChapter(chapterNumber);
                });
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
